 "failure": "capstone-v1.0 searched the help centre without the account's policy version; for a current-terms customer whose message echoed the old 14-day window, every passage placed in the prompt came from the RETIRED policy (HC-009)",
 "root_cause": "retrieval ranks by similarity; the retired article is the closest text to a question phrased in its own terms. The policy version is an account fact (entitlement), not a retrieval signal, so similarity alone cannot choose it",
 "fix": "capstone-v1.1: once check_entitlement has verified the account, the agent passes policy_version to search_help_centre (the server drops the other version), a citation filter refuses passages of the other version, and a case with no passage of the right version escalates instead of guessing",
 "regression_tests": [
  "tests/test_week12.py: 'current customer, filter on: refund_approved, only HC-008 consulted, policy_version enforced on the MCP call'",
  "tests/test_week12.py: 'filter off (v1.0): the retired policy can be cited and the guardrail catches the denial'",
  "tests/test_week12.py: 'legacy customer: refund_denied under legacy-14-day, cites HC-009 only'",
  "tests/test_week12.py: 'retired policy cited to a current account fails' (capstone_assertions.policy_version_consistent)"
 ],
